  "body": "Seeing is believing – this delightful gem is worthy of your immediate inspection!\r\n\r\nValue packed buying is on offer with this surprising and spacious circa 1970’s home ideally positioned on St Heliers northern ridgeline – offering a widespread scenic outlook and desired sunny aspect. Start your day watching the sunrise, and in the evening enjoy the panoramic view of the sunset, city and harbour lights. \r\n\r\nOnce inside, this inviting home offers the perfect opportunity to secure your place in sought-after St Heliers, with convenient access to St Heliers shopping village, beach and vibrant waterfront boulevard. Open plan living with a large entertaining deck which enhances the viewing aspect the home enjoys and offers al fresco dining and day or evening relaxation. Easy care grounds and gardens provide a private and relaxed living impression.\r\n\r\nWith thoughtful bedroom separation this is an ideal work-from-home opportunity, lock-up and leave, or a more affordable purchase for either downsizers, professional couples, or buyers looking to secure St Heliers and Glendowie College school zones. \r\n\r\nThe location is perfect, with less than a 2-minute walk to Maskell Street shops and Eastmed Medical Centre, with the benefit of public transport at your door to St Heliers and the Eastern Central Bays, and through to Auckland CBD less than 20 minutes away. \r\n\r\nThe benefit of nearby parks and walkways are bountiful with Dingle Dell Reserve, and Vellenoweth Green all within walking distance ideal for easy weekend adventures. \r\n\r\nThe owners’ retirement moves dictates sale – after 22 years of wonderful enjoyment.",
